From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:03:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] vdin: let one loopback stream read its taps in turn

A vdin read one write-back tap, so a client that wanted two taps from
one engine restarted the stream for every switch and got a fraction of
the frames. A source written by the cpu lands while the next frame is
already being written, so the first frame after a switch was torn.
